    s_k=(p_(n-k)+p_(n+k))/sqrt(2), 1<=k<=n-1.

For0<=k<=n-2 set a=n+k+1 and b=n-k, and put

    G_k=F_a-F_b,   nu_0=sqrt(2),   nu_k=1 for k>=1,
    A_k=G_k/nu_k.

Equations(1)-(2) imply [G_k,J]=0 on the whole battery. On the even prefix span, A_k acts exactly as Y between s_k and s_(k+1), and annihilates the other s_l. For k=0, G_0s_0=i sqrt(2)s_1 and G_0s_1=-i sqrt(2)s_0, which explains nu_0. For k>=1 the two distinct edges each contribute i/sqrt(2) to the outward state, giving coefficient one. No endpoint edge to p_0 or p_M is used, so the span of s_0,...,s_(n-1) is invariant for every implemented angle.

The desired real sine packet has

    beta=sum_(m=1)^(M-1) b_m p_m,
    b_m=sqrt(2/M) sin(pi m/M),
    beta=sum_(k=0)^(n-1) c_k s_k,
